  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 155 AM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nRidging continues to sit overhead bringing with it unseasonably\nwarm temperatures across the region. Today temperatures are \nforecast to peak in the upper 80s and low 90s with cloud cover \ndecreasing going into the afternoon. Dewpoints will be slightly\nhigher today especially across SEMO, far western KY and SW IL \nas the southerly/southwesterly winds advect higher dewpoints \ninto these areas. Similar highs are in the forecast for Thursday\nas clouds will return with the trough out west beginning to \nmove into the region preventing more significant warming. \nDewpoints will continue to climb into the mid and upper 60s with\nfurther moisture advection from the southerly flow Thursday.\n\nThe cold front associated with the previously discussed trough\nwill begin to make its way through the region early Friday\nmorning. Highs are forecast to only reach the mid to upper 70s\nat this time. PoPs will peak between 80-90% across the region \nduring the morning and early afternoon hours before tapering off\nslightly into Friday evening. Instability remains low for this \nrain event so no severe weather is expected, however, some \nrumbles of thunder are not out of the question. Probabilistic \nguidance continues to suggest only a 40-50% chance of an inch or\nmore of rain from this event. Concerns for flooding remain low \nat this point.\n\nCooler, seasonable temperatures (lower 70s) will continue into \nthe weekend with low PoPs (10-30%) through Saturday as the\nsystem lingers. However, drier conditions will return again \nSunday with high pressure moving in once again.",
